			<div class="content" id="post-content-637461">
									

<p>Sorry, but no, you're full of shit. IQ was actually determined as a percentage of mental age divided by chronological age when it was conceived. The formula is:</p>
<p>MA / CA * 100 = IQ</p>
<p>So say you are 16 and have the mind of a 20 year old. You have an IQ of 125. Alternately, say you are a retarded 36 year old with the mind of a 12 year old boy. Your IQ is 33. Technically the highest testable IQ would be about 2440, assuming a 5 year old (the age when school begins, and by extension testing) with the mind of a 122 year old (the age of the oldest verified human), though this is obviously an extreme example.</p>
<p>The vagaries in the test arise in how mental age is measured in an individual in a standardized fashion, which is why it is widely derided in modern times and overhauled quite a bit — and it's why it doesn't work here.</p>
<p>In any case it would be more appropriate for the purposes of the SCP to use a non-testable measure of mental activity, such as SQUID particle analysis to measure the magnetic fields of the neurological system, to imply high intelligence.</p>
<p>EDIT: I went back and read some of the other replies after writing this and realized some people have actually made most of these points already. Really should start trying to do that <em>before</em> typing.</p>

